#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# chromaticity_plot

#% text
# `chromaticity_plot(space)` draws the CIE 1931 chromaticity diagram with the gamut triangles of RGB colour spaces, or colours as points.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Spaces: `"sRGB"`, `"AdobeRGB"`, `"WideGamutRGB"`, `"ProPhotoRGB"`, `"AppleRGB"`, `"DisplayP3"`, `"Rec2020"`, `"NTSC"`, `"CIERGB"`.

#% item
# The spectral locus is the CIE 1931 standard observer's; the white point of each space is marked.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
chromaticity_plot("sRGB")
#% output
#= image("chromaticity_plot.files/chromaticity_plot-1.svgz")

#% cell
chromaticity_plot(["sRGB", "Rec2020", red, orange])
#% output
#= image("chromaticity_plot.files/chromaticity_plot-2.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
